{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018WPk85LisxZsyThchdYiHh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Prompts\n2\t\n3\tAppend-only, written by `.claude/hooks/log-prompt.sh`. Do not edit past entries.\n4\t\n5\t## 2026-09-27T22:34:59Z · ecd710da\n6\t\n7\t```text\n8\t/refine a docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md for creating a todo list app. Main objective is a simple setup but well integratable into CI with well set up test infrastructure using our ways of working @docs/rules/WOW.md for a scala pure fp cats style. The output should be colored and well structured, it should be possible to interface the todo list app with yaml and rich text directly.\n9\t\n10\tThese choices are settled, so write the spec:\n11\t- The human view is colored, structured terminal output. Rich text is a Markdown checklist the app imports and exports.\n12\t- YAML is the one store file, and the app imports and exports that same YAML.\n13\t- The MVP commands are add, list, done, and remove.\n14\t- CI is `just check`. Name that gate in the spec. The workflow file lands with the first code milestone.\n15\t\n16\tM1 scala and sbt setup\n17\tM2 cats hello world\n18\tM3 create and read todos\n19\tM4 list as table\n20\tM5 updates\n21\tM6 add colors\n22\tM7 add yaml output and argument to switch\n23\tM8 markdown checklist import and export\n24\t```\n25\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ecd710da-b418-40f6-be17-78302734a7a2","uuid":"dc362f79-ba9d-4058-865a-3a57f0fac133","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:35:12.081Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/isaiasbartelborth/Projects/hivemind/todo-list-cli/develop/docs/PROMPTS.md","content":"# Prompts\n\nAppend-only, written by `.claude/hooks/log-prompt.sh`. Do not edit past entries.\n\n## 2026-09-27T22:34:59Z · ecd710da\n\n```text\n/refine a docs/specs/SPEC.v1-todo-list-cli-mvp.md for creating a todo list app. Main objective is a simple setup but well integratable into CI with well set up test infrastructure using our ways of working @docs/rules/WOW.md for a scala pure fp cats style. The output should be colored and well structured, it should be possible to interface the todo list app with yaml and rich text directly.\n\nThese choices are settled, so write the spec:\n- The human view is colored, structured terminal output. Rich text is a Markdown checklist the app imports and exports.\n- YAML is the one store file, and the app imports and exports that same YAML.\n- The MVP commands are add, list, done, and remove.\n- CI is `just check`. Name that gate in the spec. The workflow file lands with the first code milestone.\n\nM1 scala and sbt setup\nM2 cats hello world\nM3 create and read todos\nM4 list as table\nM5 updates\nM6 add colors\nM7 add yaml output and argument to switch\nM8 markdown checklist import and export\n```\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}}}
